{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees","id":1350031,"title":"Thought experiment - sorcerer altering fruit trees","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-21T10:04:20-08:00","id":1350031,"title":"Thought experiment - sorcerer altering fruit trees","content":"Our sorcerer wants to have out of season fruit, so that he can sell them and eat them whenever he wants. He picks a peach tree famed for its deliciousness, takes a cutting, and begins to use his sorcery. He's a herbologist by trade, so he's got the relevant ability. He's got a wood elemental friend who's also a sorcerer. He's got several pieces from a giant wood elemental he helped kill. So he's got 5 rolls at the start, then adds 3 more. <br /> <br /> I plugged in the number generator: <br /> <br /> Set 1: 5, 3, 6, 7, 10, 2, 1<br /> 3 successes<br /> Set 2: 2, 5, 4, 10, 6, 7, 9<br /> 4 successes<br /> Set 3: 4, 2, 3, 6, 1, 5, 7<br /> 1 success<br /> Set 4: 9, 5, 6, 1, 10, 7, 3<br /> 4 success<br /> Set 5: 7, 1, 4, 8, 9, 3, 10<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 6: 5, 10, 6, 7, 2, 3, 8<br /> 4 successes<br /> Set 7: 4, 8, 10, 1, 3, 7, 6<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 8:<br /> 4, 6, 5, 2, 8, 7, 9<br /> 3 successes<br /> <br /> Ok. Let me get this right. I'm having difficulty 4. The plant that comes out will look obviously abornormal (the fruits look ok), and it takes, what, 10 successes to grant mutations? Difficulty 4. Now, tell me if I&quot;m doing it wrong, but Difficulty 4 means that you, shave off 4 success per roll? That means that I... Yeah, I don't get enough successes, and I fail this sorcery roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:17:48-08:00","id":1350042,"title":"","content":"I don't know how you have difficulty 4. The difficulty depends on the Finesse of the working (which you didn't specify). Finesse can be 1, 3 or 5. Let's suppose you have Finesse 4, it doesn't exist but maybe you had an agreement with the ST. It means every success that <b>meet or exceed </b>the Finesse awards you 1 success to progress on the Extended roll.<br /> <br /> In your case, you would have :<ul><li>0 success from first roll</li> <li>1 success from second roll</li> <li>0 success from third roll</li> <li>1 success from fourth roll</li> <li>2 success from fifth roll</li> <li>1 success from sixth roll</li> <li>2 success from seventh roll</li> <li>0 success from eighth roll</li> </ul>You accumulated 7 successes, so you failed the roll. I think it's fair to say that Finesse 4 doesn't exist, and you should have 3 (in which case you succeeded) or 5 (in which case you didn't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:47:05-08:00","id":1350054,"title":"","content":"Oh dear. I apologise. <br /> <br /> Well, I got fruit trees altered with finesse 3. What's the extent of the changes now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T11:16:54-08:00","id":1350067,"title":"","content":"I guess you can cross your peach with another specie (how do you write that in singular ?) to have best traits of both, so your peach could be crossed with something that grows in winter or something like that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T11:44:06-08:00","id":1350074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350067#post1350067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess you can cross your peach with another specie (how do you write that in singular ?) to have best traits of both, so your peach could be crossed with something that grows in winter or something like that</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more thinking: &quot;Ok, so you have 1 dot alchemy, something on the level of life's little luxury blends. Put that on the leaves or roots of the plant or dilute it in water and then pour it onto the tree and then it'll produce fruits by the end of a 3 day period. Fruits on demand. Not seasonal. Also, when it isn't making fruits, its storing the residual sugars and water in pods beneath the tree itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T11:47:46-08:00","id":1350075,"title":"","content":"Ok so the goal is to have out of season fruit. You're doing this by splicing a peach tree (summer harvest) with something like a clementine (winter harvest).<br /> <br /> That's an Ambition 2 Terrestial Working. You need ten successes. Check. (If successful, you'll need to spend 4XP.)<br /> <br /> At Finesses 1, the ST determines the outcome. You'll get edible fruit all year round... but it might be weird. Difficulty 1.<br /> <br /> Your working sounds like Finesse 3. You want an ever flowering magical hybrid. The ST can add quirks to make that more flavorful, but you want a great tasting cash crop. Difficulty 3.<br /> <br /> At Finesse 5 there are no quirks. You narrate every detail. Difficulty 5.<br /> <br /> You start with a Terminus of 5. Your Means adds 3. So you get 8 rolls, one roll a week.<br /> <br /> You roll Intelligence + Occult.<br /> <br /> Your Sorcerer has to have at least Occult 3 to be a Sorcerer... so if you're rolling 7 dice, I presume you have Intelligence 4.<br /> <br /> At Finesse 3, your sample rolls are successful and you have a plant that does what you want it to do... plus any quirks the ST cares to add (like making the plant look weird, for example).<br /> <br /> At Finesse 5, the highest and most difficult working, your sorcerer fails. They may be a skilled Occultist by the standards of Creation, but they're not a skilled Sorcerer by the standards of the Exalted (a Solar Sorcerer being Occult 5). An Excellency would help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T12:39:16-08:00","id":1350084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350074#post1350074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more thinking: &quot;Ok, so you have 1 dot alchemy, something on the level of life's little luxury blends. Put that on the leaves or roots of the plant or dilute it in water and then pour it onto the tree and then it'll produce fruits by the end of a 3 day period. Fruits on demand. Not seasonal. Also, when it isn't making fruits, its storing the residual sugars and water in pods beneath the tree itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not an expert on green stuff, but I think you are just making fluff, so I guess this is fine ? The thing every 3 days sound much more surnatural than an ambition 2 terrestrial should do though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T12:52:58-08:00","id":1350087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350084#post1350084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not an expert on green stuff, but I think you are just making fluff, so I guess this is fine ? The thing every 3 days sound much more surnatural than an ambition 2 terrestrial should do though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically its not 'fruit out of season'. It's 'fruit when I want it'. I like having control over stuff like this, so... yeah. Kinda wasteful, you know. One tree, making so much energy, but only fruits once or twice a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T13:01:03-08:00","id":1350090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350074#post1350074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more thinking: &amp;quot;Ok, so you have 1 dot alchemy, something on the level of life's little luxury blends. Put that on the leaves or roots of the plant or dilute it in water and then pour it onto the tree and then it'll produce fruits by the end of a 3 day period. Fruits on demand. Not seasonal. Also, when it isn't making fruits, its storing the residual sugars and water in pods beneath the tree itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Terrestrial 3 -- minor super power which augments its strongest traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T13:03:15-08:00","id":1350091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350087#post1350087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically its not 'fruit out of season'. It's 'fruit when I want it'. I like having control over stuff like this, so... yeah. Kinda wasteful, you know. One tree, making so much energy, but only fruits once or twice a year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but the Ambition 2 working specify you create a new specie (still don't know), so you can just plant a garden of it and have as much as you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T13:33:39-08:00","id":1350106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350090#post1350090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Terrestrial 3 -- minor super power which augments its strongest traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah. Storing sugars and using them for later is a superpower? <br /> <br /> Its... something plants do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T13:56:03-08:00","id":1350111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350106#post1350106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah. Storing sugars and using them for later is a superpower?<br /> <br /> Its... something plants do.</div> </div> </div> </div>JohnDoe244 is obviously talking about the property of giving whole edible fruit on demand.<br /> <br /> The very thing you're quoting refers to a power that augments a natural trait, so you're even free to spin it in terms of augmenting this &quot;something plants do&quot;.<br /> <br /> I personally think that you're overthinking it in terms of references to actual biology when that's not really an overriding concern of sorcery, but even then Ambition 3 Terrestrial seems to be about what you're after.<br /> <br /> Your sample size of one for whether or not the roll would be viable seems to be taken down by the statistical outlier of one of the rolls dramatically underperforming. If it yielded successes at the level of the rest of the rolls, it would probably come out fine.<br /> <br /> So yeah, randomness combined with pushing the around the limits of this character's likely power presents a chance that it will simply fail. That's just... the system doing its thing. If you rolled those stats towards that goal a larger number of times, you'd probably get consistently good results, and the occasional absolute disaster.<br /> <br /> That kind of thing in combination with the sunk costs of any resources put into a working that just fails translates into the characterisation of sorcerers in which they don't throw out their workings on an industrial scale or treat any given outcome for it as a given, even in cases where the game mechanics would statistically favour it turning out well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T14:00:57-08:00","id":1350114,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I should try this again sometime with an Excellency. Or a few more Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T14:14:14-08:00","id":1350121,"title":"","content":"Let's say that my sorcerer has pushed himself, moving himself to the limits of humanity, entreating demons for more power and knowledge. <br /> <br /> Set 1: 4, 8, 10, 1, 2, 6, 3, 5, 9, 7<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 2: 10, 6, 7, 3, 5, 9, 2, 4, 8, 1<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 3: 1, 10, 4, 9, 3, 2, 5, 6, 8, 7<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 4: 9, 6, 2, 7, 4, 10, 8, 3, 1, 5<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 5: 5, 6, 2, 1, 8, 9, 7, 4, 3, 10<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 6: 1, 8, 4, 7, 9, 2, 10, 5, 6, 3<br /> 5 succesess<br /> Set 7: 10, 5, 6, 1, 4, 8, 3, 2, 7, 9<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 8: 3, 9, 8, 1, 2, 7, 4, 5, 6, 10<br /> 5 successes. <br /> <br /> Ok, I think the dice gods are smiling at me. How is it now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T15:20:13-08:00","id":1350138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350121#post1350121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say that my sorcerer has pushed himself, moving himself to the limits of humanity, entreating demons for more power and knowledge.<br /> <br /> Set 1: 4, 8, 10, 1, 2, 6, 3, 5, 9, 7<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 2: 10, 6, 7, 3, 5, 9, 2, 4, 8, 1<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 3: 1, 10, 4, 9, 3, 2, 5, 6, 8, 7<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 4: 9, 6, 2, 7, 4, 10, 8, 3, 1, 5<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 5: 5, 6, 2, 1, 8, 9, 7, 4, 3, 10<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 6: 1, 8, 4, 7, 9, 2, 10, 5, 6, 3<br /> 5 succesess<br /> Set 7: 10, 5, 6, 1, 4, 8, 3, 2, 7, 9<br /> 5 successes<br /> Set 8: 3, 9, 8, 1, 2, 7, 4, 5, 6, 10<br /> 5 successes.<br /> <br /> Ok, I think the dice gods are smiling at me. How is it now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm, either you engineered the roll or you accidentally messed up your number generator command. Getting no duplicate value on 10d10 8 times in a row is roughly as likely as winning the lottery 3 consecutive times in a row.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T15:29:08-08:00","id":1350140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://qrng.anu.edu.au/Lucky.php\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://qrng.anu.edu.au/Lucky.php\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://qrng.anu.edu.au/Lucky.php\" target=\"_blank\"> http://qrng.anu.edu.au/Lucky.php </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I asked for 8 sets. 10 numbers in each numbers from 1 to 10","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T17:14:03-08:00","id":1350151,"title":"","content":"Did you select &quot;with replacements?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because selecting &quot;without replacements,&quot; which seems to be the default option, would give you exactly the problem just described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T17:19:08-08:00","id":1350152,"title":"","content":"Anyway, something I've noted before is that mortal sorcerers aren't going to be much use at high-Finesse workings -- so ironically, mortal sorcerers might end up seeming even weirder than Exalted sorcerers, because whatever their projects are have taken forms they didn't have the strength to plan out fully.<br /> <br /> You really need that Occult Excellency, at minimum, to hit those bigger numbers. (I don't think there are many Occult dice-trick Charms in print -- I think Ancient Tongue Understanding and that one upgrade from Miracles of the Solar Exalted might be the only ones? -- but there's no reason a Solar couldn't develop more.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T18:15:25-08:00","id":1350160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350151#post1350151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you select &amp;quot;with replacements?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Because selecting &amp;quot;without replacements,&amp;quot; which seems to be the default option, would give you exactly the problem just described.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well fuck. Scrap those previous calculations. I didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T19:05:53-08:00","id":1350168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350152#post1350152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I don't think there are many Occult dice-trick Charms in print -- I think Ancient Tongue Understanding and that one upgrade from Miracles of the Solar Exalted might be the only ones? -- but there's no reason a Solar couldn't develop more.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Devs intentionally didn\u2019t give many options for making sorcerous workings likelier to succeed, because even Solar sorcerers weren\u2019t intended to have a trivial time of achieving Adamant Circle workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T20:31:29-08:00","id":1350175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350168#post1350168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Devs intentionally didn\u2019t give many options for making sorcerous workings likelier to succeed, because even Solar sorcerers weren\u2019t intended to have a trivial time of achieving Adamant Circle workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have they actually stated this somewhere?<br /> <br /> Adamant Circle workings require a <i>lot</i> of successes. I don't think adding a few more dice tricks would make them trivial to achieve at all, and buying deeper into the Occult Charm tree in exchange for not having to stack quite so many Means onto your workings doesn't seem like an unreasonable tradeoff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T23:21:59-08:00","id":1350195,"title":"","content":"Also stunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T23:25:23-08:00","id":1350196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350175#post1350175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have they actually stated this somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m having trouble finding a quote where they said it directly, but one example was where <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/869500-final-pdf-what-s-new?p=869621#post869621\">Holden commented on the late patch to Fate-Shifting Solar Ar\u00eate</a>, that it wasn\u2019t intended to be the best Charm for boosting sorcerous workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T23:26:17-08:00","id":1350197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350106#post1350106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woah. Storing sugars and using them for later is a superpower? <br /> <br /> Its... something plants do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you name any fruit that goes from no blossom to fully formed fruit in three days at any time of year? Any fruit.<br /> <br /> Human beings can lift objects. It's something humans do. Lifting a 4x4 over your head is still a superpower dude.<br /> <br /> If you want to make a mystical hybrid that flowers both in and out of season, Terrestrial 2. Fruit on demand is Terrestrial 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T06:14:53-08:00","id":1350214,"title":"","content":"I've done it again. 6 dice to mean an average power sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Set 1: 10, 9, 9, 8, 7, 6<br /> Set 2: 6, 9, 2, 9, 1, 3<br /> Set 3: 5, 3, 5, 9, 10, 5<br /> Set 4: 3, 8, 9, 4, 3, 4<br /> Set 5: 9, 2, 10, 7, 7, 7<br /> Set 6: 8, 4, 6, 7, 8, 6<br /> Set 7: 3, 7, 4, 9, 2, 3<br /> Set 8: 9, 6, 10, 1, 1, 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T06:34:41-08:00","id":1350215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350197#post1350197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you name any fruit that goes from no blossom to fully formed fruit in three days at any time of year? Any fruit.<br /> <br /> Human beings can lift objects. It's something humans do. Lifting a 4x4 over your head is still a superpower dude.<br /> <br /> If you want to make a mystical hybrid that flowers both in and out of season, Terrestrial 2. Fruit on demand is Terrestrial 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. It should take at least 10 days. <br /> <br /> Aren't we granting mutations here? Not hybrids?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T06:37:47-08:00","id":1350216,"title":"","content":"Rules question on this issue: Can you use an Occult Excellency for sorcerous working? Or for that matter any long term projects? I don't recall seeing anything in the book about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T06:46:34-08:00","id":1350218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350216#post1350216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules question on this issue: Can you use an Occult Excellency for sorcerous working? Or for that matter any long term projects? I don't recall seeing anything in the book about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't need a specific mention if it falls within the general rule of being able to enhance Attribute+Ability rolls with Excellencies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T07:09:14-08:00","id":1350219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350216#post1350216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules question on this issue: Can you use an Occult Excellency for sorcerous working? Or for that matter any long term projects? I don't recall seeing anything in the book about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. You can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T07:26:30-08:00","id":1350223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350215#post1350215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right. It should take at least 10 days. <br /> <br /> Aren't we granting mutations here? Not hybrids?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which mutation? Chausse suggested you could get your results through hybridization (Terrestrial 2). You clarified that you wanted fruit on demand, and I suggested Terrestrial 3 as a minor superpower augmenting the subjects best trait.<br /> <br /> If you're got a mutation in mind that will cause the plant to bear fruit, then Terrestrial 2 is fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T07:45:26-08:00","id":1350228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350223#post1350223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which mutation? Chausse suggested you could get your results through hybridization (Terrestrial 2). You clarified that you wanted fruit on demand, and I suggested Terrestrial 3 as a minor superpower augmenting the subjects best trait.<br /> <br /> If you're got a mutation in mind that will cause the plant to bear fruit, then Terrestrial 2 is fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I see no reason to not give a homebrewed mutation that alters the plant's hormones and reproductive system such that it only fruits when you, say, paint a particular alchemical solution on its leaves. Isn't that what mutations are? 'small' alterations to the physical and mental form, too small to be a supernatural power and yet too big to be normal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T08:42:09-08:00","id":1350240,"title":"","content":"That seems more like a magical trigger to me that it seems like a mutation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T09:43:39-08:00","id":1350247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350214#post1350214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've done it again. 6 dice to mean an average power sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Set 1: 10, 9, 9, 8, 7, 6<br /> Set 2: 6, 9, 2, 9, 1, 3<br /> Set 3: 5, 3, 5, 9, 10, 5<br /> Set 4: 3, 8, 9, 4, 3, 4<br /> Set 5: 9, 2, 10, 7, 7, 7<br /> Set 6: 8, 4, 6, 7, 8, 6<br /> Set 7: 3, 7, 4, 9, 2, 3<br /> Set 8: 9, 6, 10, 1, 1, 2</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Let's see. Finesse 3. <br /> <br /> Set 1: 6 successes<br /> Set 2: 2 successes<br /> Set 3: 3 successes<br /> Set 4: 2 successes<br /> Set 5: 6 successes<br /> Set 6: 3 successes<br /> Set 7: 2 successes<br /> Set 8: 3 successes<br /> <br /> *scratches head*<br /> <br /> 6 successes accumulated. So failure in this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T10:08:36-08:00","id":1350252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350228#post1350228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I see no reason to not give a homebrewed mutation that alters the plant's hormones and reproductive system such that it only fruits when you, say, paint a particular alchemical solution on its leaves. Isn't that what mutations are? 'small' alterations to the physical and mental form, too small to be a supernatural power and yet too big to be normal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though your description is technically fitting what could be regarded as a tree with a mutated physiology, but it's so intricate in the interests of just about fitting the circumstances within that definition that I would be inclined to not allow it on principle. I think it's in the interests of sorcerous workings to take the end results at face value when coming up with Ambition levels, rather than encouraging bringing the levels down by finding the most convoluted wording necessary to make it technically fit a different enhancement.<br /> <br /> Either that or you get a tree that will grow fruit when physically triggered, but it still needs to grow and ripen as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T10:16:29-08:00","id":1350255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350247#post1350247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Let's see. Finesse 3. <br /> <br /> Set 1: 6 successes<br /> Set 2: 2 successes<br /> Set 3: 3 successes<br /> Set 4: 2 successes<br /> Set 5: 6 successes<br /> Set 6: 3 successes<br /> Set 7: 2 successes<br /> Set 8: 3 successes<br /> <br /> *scratches head*<br /> <br /> 6 successes accumulated. So failure in this.</div> </div> </div> </div>So protip: 2 dice is approximately equal to 1 success.<br /> <br /> A 6 dice sorcerer, on an average roll, is not going to get ten successes on eight rolls at difficulty 3. It's possible, but it's not happening on an average roll. Consider stunting, spending Willpower or adding more Means.<br /> <br /> Your mortal sorcerer is going for Finesse 1 Workings. With their Excellent Occult skills, the Exalted can master the arts of sorcery and be more precise in their miracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-22-2019, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T10:28:08-08:00","id":1350256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350252#post1350252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as though your description is technically fitting what could be regarded as a tree with a mutated physiology, but it's so intricate in the interests of just about fitting the circumstances within that definition that I would be inclined to not allow it on principle. I think it's in the interests of sorcerous workings to take the end results at face value when coming up with Ambition levels, rather than encouraging bringing the levels down by finding the most convoluted wording necessary to make it technically fit a different enhancement.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting stance. I don't disagree, but I'm not sure I agree either.<br /> <br /> Take, for example, flight. Clearly a Celestial 2 supernatural ability. But the Wings mutation exists -- it's an actual, published mutation. And you can bestow mutations at Terrestial 2.<br /> <br /> Would you allow the Wings mutation at Terrestrial 2?<br /> <br /> I think I would, but maybe insist on Finesse 5 for the five-dot Merit. So then Celestial 2... does that allow for flight without the drawbacks of Wings? I wouldn't be happy having no drawbacks at all... but I don't think it should take going up an entire Circle for a purely cosmetic change. But I also think Sorcery should serve the story rather than be a vector for kewl powaz. But then it's easy to base a story around wanting the power of flight (Perdido Street Station is an excellent novel, good Exalted inspiration for any Twilight, Alchemical or Guarda bird characters).<br /> <br /> So... I don't know. But it's an interesting point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T10:57:36-08:00","id":1350261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350247#post1350247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Let's see. Finesse 3.<br /> <br /> Set 1: 6 successes<br /> Set 2: 2 successes<br /> Set 3: 3 successes<br /> Set 4: 2 successes<br /> Set 5: 6 successes<br /> Set 6: 3 successes<br /> Set 7: 2 successes<br /> Set 8: 3 successes<br /> <br /> *scratches head*<br /> <br /> 6 successes accumulated. So failure in this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually for Finesse 3 you accumulated 11 successes with those rolls.<br /> <br /> 6 successes on the roll net you 4 accumulated sucesses.<br /> <br /> With Finesse (same as difficulty for extended rolls, such as crafting or feats of strength) you have to remember that the success that brings you over the threshold counts as a success.<br /> <br /> So for Finesse 3, the 3rd, 4th, 5th and 6th successes count for accumulation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T11:00:37-08:00","id":1350262,"title":"","content":"So let's try that again. <br /> <br /> Let's say that our sorcerer has decided to put in some extra effort, and got lucky. Maybe he got exalted, or got a blessing from a god, or whatever. But for now, let's say he's got an occult excellency. 6 dice are now 12 dice. Same as before. 8 rolls. <br /> <br /> Set 1: 3, 4, 1, 2, 9, 2, 3, 1, 3, 7, 7, 8<br /> Successes: 4<br /> <br /> Set 2: 9, 10, 7, 8, 2, 6, 7, 3, 9, 2, 2, 10<br /> Successes: 9<br /> <br /> Set 3: 5, 9, 9, 4, 8, 7, 1, 5, 1, 7, 3, 2<br /> Successes: 5<br /> <br /> Set 4: 8, 3, 2, 10, 3, 10, 6, 6, 7, 7, 4, 1<br /> Successes: 7<br /> <br /> Set 5: 4, 5, 2, 8, 6, 8, 4, 1, 6, 1, 1, 9<br /> Successes: 3<br /> <br /> Set 6: 8, 5, 2, 5, 1, 2, 7, 2, 9, 3, 7, 9<br /> Successes: 5<br /> <br /> Set 7: 1, 10, 4, 8, 1, 10, 3, 4, 9, 6, 10, 4<br /> Successe: 8<br /> <br /> Set 8: 7, 9, 9, 10, 3, 9, 4, 1, 3, 3, 7, 5<br /> Successes: 7<br /> <br /> That's with an occult excellency. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T11:12:17-08:00","id":1350266,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a><br /> <br /> 32 successes.<br /> <br /> The formula per roll is Net Success = Successes - (Finesse -1)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T11:35:04-08:00","id":1350272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350255#post1350255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So protip: 2 dice is approximately equal to 1 success.<br /> <br /> A 6 dice sorcerer, on an average roll, is not going to get ten successes on eight rolls at difficulty 3. It's possible, but it's not happening on an average roll. Consider stunting, spending Willpower or adding more Means.<br /> <br /> Your mortal sorcerer is going for Finesse 1 Workings. With their Excellent Occult skills, the Exalted can master the arts of sorcery and be more precise in their miracles.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on John's point<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Workings have a base interval of 1 week, so there is no reason whatsoever for a mortal sorcerer not to put a willpower on every roll (they have a full week to recover it each time). This means your un-excellencied roll with 6 successes could have gotten 8 extra successes with no chance involved, bringing you to 14 successes and clearing the Ambition 2 bar.<br /> <br /> Then a simple 1 point stunt on each roll would give an extra 16 dice :<br /> <br /> roll result : 9,8,8,3,1,8,5,1,5,9,8,2,7,1,9,5<br /> Successes : 8<br /> <br /> bringing you to 22 successes and clearing the Ambition 3 bar.<br /> <br /> So maybe a mortal NPC isn't meant to achieve Ambition 3 Finesse 3 Terrestrial Workings, but it's definitely within the reach of a mortal PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 11-22-2019, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T16:18:09-08:00","id":1350337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350256#post1350256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting stance. I don't disagree, but I'm not sure I agree either.<br /> <br /> Take, for example, flight. Clearly a Celestial 2 supernatural ability. But the Wings mutation exists -- it's an actual, published mutation. And you can bestow mutations at Terrestial 2.<br /> <br /> Would you allow the Wings mutation at Terrestrial 2?<br /> <br /> I think I would, but maybe insist on Finesse 5 for the five-dot Merit. So then Celestial 2... does that allow for flight without the drawbacks of Wings? I wouldn't be happy having no drawbacks at all... but I don't think it should take going up an entire Circle for a purely cosmetic change. But I also think Sorcery should serve the story rather than be a vector for kewl powaz. But then it's easy to base a story around wanting the power of flight (Perdido Street Station is an excellent novel, good Exalted inspiration for any Twilight, Alchemical or Guarda bird characters).<br /> <br /> So... I don't know. But it's an interesting point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd kind of respond to that in terms of the end in question for having the Wings Merit being having the Wings Merit as opposed to the function the Merit is applied to. In addition to granting that I could have used a more tight wording if I was writing that as a rule rather than is having a conversation.<br /> <br /> (I'm not saying that as a dig, in really just letting myself of the hook for overlooking a technical point)<br /> <br /> Still, that's not really the case for the example in question. It's really a lot more like if somebody wrote up a custom Merit that I judged to be tailored too much to resembling a supernatural power or otherwise violating what I regarded as their standards and limits for the sake of getting an effect at a lower level than it should.<br /> <br /> Or really, just the overall idea that there are some things that are extreme enough that even if presenting them as souped up biology is perfectly sensible as the explanation for how they work, they belong in a higher Circle or Ambition in interests of things like game balance and preserving the feel of sorcery and the setting.<br /> <br /> Urrgh, this is bringing up a lot of Mage: the Awakening argument memories. &quot;Look, <i>technically</i> I can phrase a process for time travel that would fall under the Practice of Compelling.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T17:18:32-08:00","id":1350351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350256#post1350256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting stance. I don't disagree, but I'm not sure I agree either.<br /> <br /> Take, for example, flight. Clearly a Celestial 2 supernatural ability. But the Wings mutation exists -- it's an actual, published mutation. And you can bestow mutations at Terrestial 2.<br /> <br /> Would you allow the Wings mutation at Terrestrial 2?<br /> <br /> I think I would, but maybe insist on Finesse 5 for the five-dot Merit. So then Celestial 2... does that allow for flight without the drawbacks of Wings? I wouldn't be happy having no drawbacks at all... but I don't think it should take going up an entire Circle for a purely cosmetic change. But I also think Sorcery should serve the story rather than be a vector for kewl powaz. But then it's easy to base a story around wanting the power of flight (Perdido Street Station is an excellent novel, good Exalted inspiration for any Twilight, Alchemical or Guarda bird characters).<br /> <br /> So... I don't know. But it's an interesting point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would allow something like wings at Terrestrial 2 and flighting at Celestial 2. The exp cost and the work to make it happen prevent it from being a minor thing. 4 xp to gain flight is right in line with an athletics charm. Tack some rules on it depending on Finesse, even flight without wings might cost a willpower or be as taxing as running. Having wings all the time is a pain regardless. More so if your magic is just used to grow giant wings to support you body vs making you lighter. Or perhaps making your bones more brittle. Published versions are just guidelines not hard rules. If the player wants exactly as published, then Finesse 5. Otherwise it is a gamble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T23:18:10-08:00","id":1350397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350196#post1350196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m having trouble finding a quote where they said it directly, but one example was where <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/869500-final-pdf-what-s-new?p=869621#post869621\">Holden commented on the late patch to Fate-Shifting Solar Ar\u00eate</a>, that it wasn\u2019t intended to be the best Charm for boosting sorcerous workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, but:<br /> 1) Fate-Shifting Solar Arete is a remarkably powerful effect, so I don't think this is the same as saying &quot;no more dice tricks for Occult at all&quot; and<br /> 2) I think the main issue here is not even that it's too powerful, but rather &quot;it's really absurd for the best sorcery booster to be a <i>Larceny</i> Charm.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T23:39:45-08:00","id":1350398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350266#post1350266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> <br /> 32 successes.<br /> <br /> The formula per roll is Net Success = Successes - (Finesse -1)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which goes to show how fucking ridiculous the Exalted are even with excellencies alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T01:48:43-08:00","id":1350405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350397#post1350397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see, but:<br /> 1) Fate-Shifting Solar Arete is a remarkably powerful effect, so I don't think this is the same as saying &amp;quot;no more dice tricks for Occult at all&amp;quot; and<br /> 2) I think the main issue here is not even that it's too powerful, but rather &amp;quot;it's really absurd for the best sorcery booster to be a <i>Larceny</i> Charm.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What larceny charm? The one that lets you bank successes? I thought there were some really hard limits on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T02:09:52-08:00","id":1350406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350272#post1350272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To expand on John's point<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Workings have a base interval of 1 week, so there is no reason whatsoever for a mortal sorcerer not to put a willpower on every roll (they have a full week to recover it each time). This means your un-excellencied roll with 6 successes could have gotten 8 extra successes with no chance involved, bringing you to 14 successes and clearing the Ambition 2 bar.<br /> <br /> Then a simple 1 point stunt on each roll would give an extra 16 dice :<br /> <br /> roll result : 9,8,8,3,1,8,5,1,5,9,8,2,7,1,9,5<br /> Successes : 8<br /> <br /> bringing you to 22 successes and clearing the Ambition 3 bar.<br /> <br /> So maybe a mortal NPC isn't meant to achieve Ambition 3 Finesse 3 Terrestrial Workings, but it's definitely within the reach of a mortal PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry.... so what you're saying is, I left out the stunts and the willpower, with each stunt giving me 2 extra dice per interval, and the willpower giving me one extra success per interval?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T04:34:15-08:00","id":1350421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350406#post1350406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry.... so what you're saying is, I left out the stunts and the willpower, with each stunt giving me 2 extra dice per interval, and the willpower giving me one extra success per interval?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah pretty much. You'd have to roll the stunt dice to be sure, but on a Terminus 8 that's an extra 16 successes on average that you missed out on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T04:51:02-08:00","id":1350422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350405#post1350405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What larceny charm? The one that lets you bank successes? I thought there were some really hard limits on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's Fate-Shifting Solar Arete. It lets you choose a number from 2 to 5 to treat as a 10 for one non-extended roll per full night rest. 2 numbers with a repurchase at essence 4.<br /> <br /> So it lowers the odds of failure by removing possible failure numbers, and raises the success count by turning those failures into double successes.<br /> <br /> It basically lets you dramatically raise your odds/success count for one roll per day, regardless of what Ability is part of that roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T05:33:05-08:00","id":1350426,"title":"","content":"And tell me if I'm wrong. Basically, each interval you roll successes, Then minus it from either 4 or 2 successes, depending on the finesse you chose. And then you add them up, and see if you get enough successes to hit the ambition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T08:18:56-08:00","id":1350441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350426#post1350426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And tell me if I'm wrong. Basically, each interval you roll successes, Then minus it from either 4 or 2 successes, depending on the finesse you chose. And then you add them up, and see if you get enough successes to hit the ambition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds about right.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T08:29:36-08:00","id":1350442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350426#post1350426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And tell me if I'm wrong. Basically, each interval you roll successes, Then minus it from either 4 or 2 successes, depending on the finesse you chose. And then you add them up, and see if you get enough successes to hit the ambition.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can go with Finesse 1 and subtract nothing too. You can also choose to lower the Finesse mid-project, if you think you will not make it with the current Finesse, but that has some added consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T08:56:19-08:00","id":1350446,"title":"","content":"Ok. Let's see... Terrestrial 2 is goal number 20<br /> <br /> Celestial 2 is goal number 30. Let's say that I wish to create a pond whose water when sprinkled on a plant or animal makes it grow like its in the frickin' garden of eden. Granting mutations for hardiness, increased size, increased deliciousness, and more fertility and growth rate. So I take months to take it, instead of weeks. So in the end, I have... 9 rolls? Then I add in a spell I know that warps or transforms life. Either summoning the harvest or sprouting shackles of doom. Let's say my sorcerer has accrued an entire library of sorcerous materials and ingredients. That's 11 rolls in total. <br /> <br /> Now looking back at things... I have extra 2 dice from stunts. My sorcerer has 6 dice in total, and now has 8. And then add in the months component.... <br /> <br /> 8 dice. 11 rolls. One extra success due to willpower expenditure. Finesse 3, with an added difficulty due to celestial scale working. Minus away 4 successes per roll. <br /> <br /> Let's roll. <br /> <br /> Set 1: 1, 8, 9, 8, 4, 3, 1, 8<br /> Successes: 5<br /> <br /> Set 2: 3, 8, 9, 8, 1, 2, 7, 8<br /> Successes: 6<br /> <br /> Set 3: 9, 7, 7, 3, 8, 5, 6, 6<br /> Successes: 5<br /> <br /> Set 4: 2, 1, 10, 3, 3, 6, 3, 5<br /> Successes: 3<br /> <br /> Set 5: 9, 9, 8, 4, 5, 2, 4, 6<br /> Successes: 4<br /> <br /> Set 6: 4, 10, 9, 9, 3, 8, 8, 8<br /> Successes: 8<br /> <br /> Set 7: 10, 1, 6, 5, 5, 5, 5, 6<br /> Successes: 3<br /> <br /> Set 8: 1, 8, 10, 4, 4, 3, 2, 9<br /> Successes: 5<br /> <br /> Set 9: 9, 1, 5, 1, 7, 3, 2, 6<br /> Successes: 3<br /> <br /> Set 10: 9, 2, 4, 9, 9, 2, 6, 7<br /> Successes: 5<br /> <br /> Set 11: 8, 4, 3, 8, 7, 3, 3, 5<br /> Successes: 4<br /> <br /> Number of accumulated successes: 10<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Failure. <br /> <br /> Presuming that I'm the best of the best, 10 dice, and 2 extra from a stunt.... <br /> <br /> Set 1: 9, 3, 2, 9, 5, 4, 1, 5, 9, 7, 1, 6 (5 successes)<br /> Set 2: 2, 8, 10, 9, 3, 10, 9, 4, 7, 10, 10, 8 (14 successes)<br /> Set 3: 8, 5, 9, 8, 1, 8, 6, 7, 4, 6, 2, 5 (6 successes)<br /> Set 4: 7, 10, 7, 8, 9, 5, 4, 4, 2, 4, 5, 10 (8 successes)<br /> Set 5: 5, 2, 5, 2, 2, 6, 10, 1, 5, 2, 2, 5 (3 successes)<br /> Set 6: 1, 5, 8, 6, 9, 8, 5, 7, 6, 2, 2, 6 (5 successes)<br /> Set 7: 4, 4, 6, 9, 7, 2, 7, 7, 3, 4, 4, 6 (5 successes)<br /> Set 8: 6, 10, 7, 5, 6, 4, 7, 3, 8, 8, 3, 10 (9 successes)<br /> Set 9: 6, 8, 7, 2, 5, 8, 3, 6, 1, 5, 2, 6 (4 succesess)<br /> Set 10: 3, 9, 9, 3, 8, 3, 4, 6, 8, 1, 9, 8 (7 successes)<br /> Set 11: 8, 8, 8, 3, 10, 4, 5, 7, 5, 9, 2, 6 (8 successes)<br /> <br /> 1 + 10 + 2 + 4 + 1 + 1 + 5 + 3 + 4 = 31<br /> <br /> Everyone clap, for my hypothetical sorcerer has managed to create a celestial 2 working! His kingdom shall be known far and wide for the bountiful crops they have! <br /> <br /> He was, of course, utterly saved by the set 2, without which he would have failed miserably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T10:22:59-08:00","id":1350457,"title":"","content":"I'm unsure what you are trying to achieve in this thread. I got your questionning about what circle would be a good choice for your working, but chaining rolls until you succeed does not make sense in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T10:24:54-08:00","id":1350458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350457#post1350457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unsure what you are trying to achieve in this thread. I got your questionning about what circle would be a good choice for your working, but chaining rolls until you succeed does not make sense in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. Is just that I have a poor understanding of exalted system. Right now, spreading my wings and shaking things up? I feel much more enlightened. Thanks for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T12:07:51-08:00","id":1350481,"title":"","content":"Also I still don't understand how you count your successes : Successes on rolls with a difficulty does count the threshold success. For example, on Finesse 3, making 5 successes give you 2 successes on the extended roll. I still don't get how you subtract 4 from your rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T13:03:36-08:00","id":1350496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350481#post1350481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I still don't understand how you count your successes : Successes on rolls with a difficulty does count the threshold success. For example, on Finesse 3, making 5 successes give you 2 successes on the extended roll. I still don't get how you subtract 4 from your rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually the case. On page 189 of the core book it states:<br /> &quot;When determining a character\u2019s current success total, count<br /> only those successes that meet or exceed the action\u2019s difficulty.<br /> For example, a player attempting an extended action<br /> with difficulty 3 who rolled four successes would accumulate<br /> two cumulative successes toward her goal number.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","name":"Speedbump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T15:03:51-08:00","id":1350523,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm sorry I wrote down the same thing than you and then I successfully made a wrong calculation. I of course meant than with finesse 3, rolling 5 successes give you 3 successes on the extended roll. Sorry for the confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T15:38:59-08:00","id":1350529,"title":"","content":"I feel like a mortal with Int 3 and occult 3 is really going to struggle with a celestial working, even with lots of resources to help. If I was a mortal I'd really try to stack on the bonuses in a way exalted don't need to. Get gods to help, trade favors for mystical aid, summon a demon and bargain with it. Also a bonus die if you can wiggle a speciality into it. Exalted can cover all this with just bigger dice pools. Mortals need aid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T16:20:58-08:00","id":1350536,"title":"","content":"I had been holding off a more detailed reply because was playing with random.org to see how well effective different dice pools actually turn out to be. With a &quot;bare minimum&quot; dice pool of 6 (3 Occult, Int 1, Stunt 2) and no means I succeeded ambition 1 and 2 finesse 1 workings every time, ambition 1 finesse 2 7 times out of 10 and ambition 2 finesse 2 1 time out of 10.<br /> <br /> Stepping things up to 8 dice (Occult 3-4, Int 2-3, Stunt 2) without means ambition 2 finesse 2 was 7/10 and ambition 3 finesse 1 was the same. Finesse 3 was only a reached once but that outlier was good for ambitions 1 and 2.<br /> <br /> Getting up to the original premise of an 8 dice character going all out with means. With 3 means and spending willpower on every roll all I got 10/10 for terrestrial workings at finesse 1. 10/10 for ambition 1 and 2 at finesse 2. 7/10 for ambition 3 a finesse 1. 8/10 for ambition 1 at finesse 3. 4/10 for ambition 2 finesse 3. And one set of rolls that would have succeeded at a Celestial ambition 1 finesse 1. Surprisingly terrestrial ambition 3 finesse 3 was never hit.<br /> <br /> I do intend to keep messing around with this for higher values, but I don't post that often so I might as well throw this out before I get destracted by something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","name":"Speedbump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T18:03:49-08:00","id":1350557,"title":"","content":"Finesse 2 isn't a thing - you can do 1, 3, or 5.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T18:20:32-08:00","id":1350560,"title":"","content":"Finesse 1 = Player decides the basic effect, ST decides the overall effect. Finesse 3 = Player decides most of the effect, ST tweaks slightly. Finesse 5 = Player writes the effect, ST approves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T19:13:49-08:00","id":1350567,"title":"","content":"Yea that's my mistake. When doing my test I made a 3X3 grid to record my results. However I did actually measure finesse accurately even though I got the terms wrong.I did in fact track the amount of successes -2 for what I called finesses 2 (and should have called finesse 3) and the amount of successes -4 for what I called finessse3 (and should have called finesse 5) and I did deliberately disregard those rolls that 'would have' been failures. But I accept that after I've made such a basic error there is no reason for you to trust me any further. Apologies for the confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","name":"Speedbump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T21:12:16-08:00","id":1350577,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the math all the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T22:03:24-08:00","id":1350582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350446#post1350446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Let's see... Terrestrial 2 is goal number 20<br /> <br /> Celestial 2 is goal number 30. Let's say that I wish to create a pond whose water when sprinkled on a plant or animal makes it grow like its in the frickin' garden of eden. Granting mutations for hardiness, increased size, increased deliciousness, and more fertility and growth rate. So I take months to take it, instead of weeks. So in the end, I have... 9 rolls? Then I add in a spell I know that warps or transforms life. Either summoning the harvest or sprouting shackles of doom. Let's say my sorcerer has accrued an entire library of sorcerous materials and ingredients. That's 11 rolls in total.<br /> <br /> Now looking back at things... I have extra 2 dice from stunts. My sorcerer has 6 dice in total, and now has 8. And then add in the months component....<br /> <br /> 8 dice. 11 rolls. One extra success due to willpower expenditure. Finesse 3, with an added difficulty due to celestial scale working. Minus away 4 successes per roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>The base terminus for sorcerous workings is 5, not 8. Adding months + known spell + exotic material only brings this to 8, not 11.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 11-24-2019, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T23:29:20-08:00","id":1350590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350031-thought-experiment-sorcerer-altering-fruit-trees?p=1350582#post1350582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The base terminus for sorcerous workings is 5, not 8. Adding months + known spell + exotic material only brings this to 8, not 11.</div> </div> </div> </div>Including the ones when I was creating terrestrial workings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T01:18:40-08:00","id":1350600,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting if you are doing a working of a Circle that is higher than the one you are initiated, Difficulty increase by 2 and the intervals of time increase as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}